-- title:
--   Regularity outside S ascends along a constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K\subseteq K'$ be algebraically closed fields and let $F/K$, $F'/K'$ be field extensions equipped with compatible algebra maps $K\to K'$, $F\to F'$, $K\to F'$ forming scalar towers $K\to K'\to F'$ and $K\to F\to F'$, with $K'$ and $F$ acting on $F'$ commutingly. Assume $F/K$ and $F'/K'$ are curves in the sense of `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero element has a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place is its order there, each place has residue field finite over the base field, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one over the top field; assume further that $F$ is essentially of finite type over $K$ and $F'$ over $K'$. Assume there is $x\in F$ transcendental over $K$ with $F$ finite over $K(x)$, likewise $x'\in F'$ over $K'$, and that the $K'$-subfield of $F'$ generated by the image of $F$ is all of $F'$. Let $S$ be a set of places of $F/K$ (valuation subrings of $F$, proper, containing $K$, and principal ideal rings) and let $\omega\in\Omega_{F/K}$ be such that for every place $v\notin S$ one has $\omega=f\cdot d\pi_v$ for some $f\in\mathcal O_v$, where $\pi_v$ is the chosen uniformiser at $v$. Then for every place $w$ of $F'/K'$ such that no $v\in S$ satisfies $\mathcal O_w\cap F=\mathcal O_v$ (preimage along $F\to F'$), the image `KaehlerDifferential.map K K' F F' ω` is likewise of the form $g\cdot d\pi_w$ with $g\in\mathcal O_w$.
--
--   This is the ascent, along a constant field extension of algebraically closed constant fields, of the property of a differential being regular away from a prescribed set of places; no condition is imposed at the places of $S$, and correspondingly no bound on pole orders is asserted at the places above them. It is used in the analysis of $q$-expansions of cusp forms, where regularity of a differential on a curve over a larger algebraically closed constant field is deduced from regularity over the smaller one.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_isRegularAt_map_of_forall_isRegularAt_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed.lean

import Mathlib
